\begin{subfigure}{0.32\linewidth}\centering\captionsetup{margin={4.90mm,0mm}}\caption{Gaussian model}\label{fig:flicker_a}\includegraphics[width=\linewidth]{figures/flicker_a.pdf}\end{subfigure}\hfill%
\begin{subfigure}{0.32\linewidth}\centering\captionsetup{margin={4.90mm,0mm}}\caption{GG model}\label{fig:flicker_b}\includegraphics[width=\linewidth]{figures/flicker_b.pdf}\end{subfigure}\hfill%
\begin{subfigure}{0.32\linewidth}\centering\captionsetup{margin={4.90mm,0mm}}\caption{Binarised angiogram}\label{fig:flicker_c}\includegraphics[width=\linewidth]{figures/flicker_c.pdf}\end{subfigure}\\
\begin{subfigure}{0.32\linewidth}\centering\captionsetup{margin={4.90mm,0mm}}\caption{Gaussian model}\label{fig:flicker_d}\includegraphics[width=\linewidth]{figures/flicker_d.pdf}\end{subfigure}\hfill%
\begin{subfigure}{0.32\linewidth}\centering\captionsetup{margin={4.90mm,0mm}}\caption{GG model}\label{fig:flicker_e}\includegraphics[width=\linewidth]{figures/flicker_e.pdf}\end{subfigure}\hfill%
\begin{subfigure}{0.32\linewidth}\centering\captionsetup{margin={4.90mm,0mm}}\caption{Binarised angiogram}\label{fig:flicker_f}\includegraphics[width=\linewidth]{figures/flicker_f.pdf}\end{subfigure}\\
\begin{subfigure}{0.32\linewidth}\centering\captionsetup{margin={5.40mm,0mm}}\caption{Angiogram intensity}\label{fig:flicker_g}\includegraphics[width=\linewidth]{figures/flicker_g.pdf}\end{subfigure}\hfill%
\begin{subfigure}{0.32\linewidth}\centering\captionsetup{margin={2.70mm,-2.70mm}}\caption{Mean angiogram intensity}\label{fig:flicker_h}\includegraphics[width=\linewidth]{figures/flicker_h.pdf}\end{subfigure}\hfill%
\begin{subfigure}[t]{0.32\linewidth}\centering\raisebox{12pt}{\includegraphics[width=0.6\linewidth]{figures/flicker_legend.pdf}}\end{subfigure}
\caption{Functional flicker stimulation results.~(a--c) Vessel diameter time series pre- and post-stimulation for (a) Gaussian model, (b) Generalised Gaussian model, and (c) binarised mask (BW-5), across five vessels. All measurements used the mean intensity projection. Vertical dashed lines indicate stimulation onset and offset.~(d--f) Mean diameter per vessel before (dark bars) and after (light bars) stimulation for each method. Veins are shown in blue/cyan and arteries in dark/light red. Significance levels: $^{**}p < 0.01$, $^{***}p < 0.001$.~(g) Angiogram intensity time series and (h) mean angiogram intensity per vessel pre- and post-stimulation.}
\label{fig:flicker}
\end{figure}

The binary mask based method showed uniformly positive per-vessel correlations, with an overall correlation of $\rho = 0.526$ ($p < 0.0005$; Fig.~\ref{fig:scatter_intensity}c). The Gaussian and GG models yielded overall correlations of $\rho = -0.101$ and $\rho = -0.098$, respectively (Fig.~\ref{fig:scatter_intensity}a,b). The angiogram intensity time series (Fig.~\ref{fig:flicker}g) showed a visible decline in angiogram intensity throughout the duration of the DyC-OCT scan across all five vessels. The mean intensity comparison pre- and post-stimulation (Fig.~\ref{fig:flicker}h) confirmed that the decrease was significant for all vessels, ranging from $-13.6\%$ to $-19.8\%$ (Table~\ref{tab:flicker}). 

